 "description": "<p>Basaltø 2.04&nbsp;Marine Monitoring Station&nbsp;is a standard hydrographic station&nbsp;in Young Sund,&nbsp;North-East Greenland. The station is part of the MarinBasis monitoring program. The purpose of the marine monitoring program is to register specific&nbsp;physical properties&nbsp;of the sea water column,&nbsp;such as temperature and&nbsp;salinity,&nbsp;at the same geographical location&nbsp;once every year, and compare these repeated registrations&nbsp;with&nbsp;previous years' recordings. Hydrographic measurements are&nbsp;typical carried out with a CTD instrument (Conductivity, Temperature, and Depth). The hydrographic station is&nbsp;monitored one time each year&nbsp;in July/August.</p>",
